# Generated output is ignored inside the component that generates it —
# datad/.gitignore covers the appliance's build, dist and target trees,
# datad/fuzz/.gitignore its corpus workspace's, and ctrld/.gitignore the
# management server's _build, deps and generated assets. Nothing writes any of
# them at the repository root, and none of them is ignored here on purpose: an
# artifact tree appearing beside the two components means something ran in the
# wrong directory, and the right answer to that is for git to say so.
/book/book/

# Crash dumps are the exception, because neither runtime chooses where to drop
# one — each writes it into whatever directory it was invoked from, which is a
# property of the invocation and not of the component. Both patterns are
# therefore unanchored: an appliance-side compiler crash and a BEAM crash are
# equally uncommittable wherever they land.
rustc-ice-*.txt
erl_crash.dump

# Key material must never reach a commit, whatever path it is dropped at: the
# development signing keys under datad/build/dev-keys, the development CA under
# datad/build/dev-ca, and any TLS-inspection CA or private key an operator
# points the build at. These are catch-all patterns rather than specific paths
# precisely because the paths are configurable.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.gpg
*-ca.crt
